+# application-lifecycle — delta
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+### Requirement: Exhaustive teardown cleanup
+Flask SHALL invoke every registered teardown callback and every receiver of the
+corresponding teardown signal during request and application-context teardown,
+even if prior teardown work raises an exception. After cleanup completes, Flask
+SHALL raise all collected teardown errors as an exception group when supported
+by the running Python version; on older versions it MAY raise the first
+collected error. Flask SHALL restore context-local state before the error
+leaves teardown.
+
+#### Scenario: Multiple failing request teardown participants
+- WHEN request teardown callbacks or request-tearing-down signal receivers
+  raise exceptions
+- THEN all registered participants are attempted, the failures are retained,
+  and no request or application context remains active after teardown
+
+#### Scenario: Multiple failing application teardown participants
+- WHEN application teardown callbacks or appcontext-tearing-down signal
+  receivers raise exceptions
+- THEN all registered participants are attempted, the failures are retained,
+  and no application context remains active after teardown
+
+## MODIFIED Requirements
+
+## REMOVED Requirements
